    "created_at": "2018-08-17T07:34:38Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-08-17T07:34:38Z",
    "body": "@yuki3 the rationale is that if an event listener in a shadow tree calls a \"global function\", that global function then has access to the shadow tree through `window.event`, breaking encapsulation.\r\n\r\nTechnically this applies to composed events as well, however in that case the global function could have obtained a reference to the `Event` object earlier on easily enough as well.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
